          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#strong_generation Strong generation
          %p
            In a well-pointed topos, the terminal object is even an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+generator"} extremal generator
          %ul
            %li
              equivalently: the global section functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(1,-)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative functor
            %li
              equivalently: if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
              induces a bijection
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(1,A) \cong E(1,B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is an isomorphism.
            %li
              equivalently: if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↣
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:A\rightarrowtail B
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              such that every global element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to B
              factors through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              is an isomorphism.
          %p
            To prove the last version, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_A : B\to \Omega
            be the classifying map of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊤
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top : B\to \Omega
            be the classifying map of the maximal subobject. If every global element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:1\to B
            factors through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi A
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mo ⊤
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_A b = \top b
            for all such
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mo ⊤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_A = \top
            by well-pointedness, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is isomorphic to the maximal subobject.
          %p
            Note that in any category with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizers"} equalizers
          %h3#boolean_properties Boolean properties
          %p
            Assuming that one accepts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            in one's metalogic, a well-pointed topos is also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↣
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\rightarrowtail A
            be a subobject and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg U
            its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting complement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg U
            are precisely the global elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            that do not factor through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            factors through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \cup \neg U
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\cup \neg U = A
          %p
            Similarly, a well-pointed topos is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-valued+topos"} two-valued
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global elements
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot
            (and these are distinct, by nondegeneracy) – or equivalently, the only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subterminal+objects"} subterminal objects
            are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            has only one global element, so it only has two possible global elements.
          %p
            Finally, a well-pointed topos has
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+supports"} split supports
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            must be either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            by two-valuedness. If it is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≅
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\cong 0
            also and its support is split. Otherwise,
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≇
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ncong 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inl
                    %mo ,
                    %mi inr
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inl, inr : A \rightrightarrows A+A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            by disjointness. Since
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≇
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ncong 0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inl
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi inr
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inl\neq inr
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:1\to A
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inl
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi inr
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inl a \neq inr a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            splits the support of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p Conversely, we have the following:
          %p
          #BooleanTwovaluedSupportssplit.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is nondegenerate (i.e.
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ≇
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\ncong 0
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              This is Proposition 9.33 on p. 314 of
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Johnstone77"} Johnstone, Topos Theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Freyd70"} Freyd
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↣
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\rightarrowtail B
              be a monomorphism such that every global element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              factors through it. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_B A
              is a subterminal object, hence either
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi B
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\forall_B A = \exists_B \neg A
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg A
              is well-supported. Hence, since supports split,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg A
              has a global element, which is impossible since every global element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              factors through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi B
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_B A = 1
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A=B
          %p
            Thus, in external classical logic, a topos is well-pointed if and only if it is nondegenerate, Boolean, two-valued, and has split supports. In particular, a nondegenerate two-valued topos satisfying the external
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            is well-pointed.
          %h3#logical_properties Logical properties
          %p
            The main point of a well-pointed topos in logic is the equivalence of
            %em external
            and
            %em internal
            properties. In particular, a statement in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of the topos will be satisfied if and only if it holds for all global terms. (For the ‘only if’ part, it is necessary that the topos be nondegenerate.)
          %h3#wellpointedness_and_concrete_categories Well-pointedness and concrete categories
          %p
            The category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            of sets and functions is both well-pointed and concrete. However, not every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            is a well-pointed category: the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Field
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
            and field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            is concrete, but is not well-pointed because it doesn’t have a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            aren’t defined to be concrete.
          %p
            The distinction between well-pointed categories and concrete categories is the distinction between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+elements"} global elements
            in a concrete category, as it is not true that elements and global elements (if they exist) coincide in general.
          %h2#general Generalizations
          %h3#in_constructive_mathematics In constructive mathematics
          %p
            To maintain this logical result in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            (that is, without excluded middle in the metalogic), one must add the following requirements:
          %ol
            %li
              the terminal object is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indecomposable+object"} indecomposable
            %li
              the terminal object is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
          %p
            These are analogues, for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantification"} existential quantification
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/falsehood"} falsehood
          %p Incidentally, a well-pointed topos in a constructive metalogic is still “two-valued” in the sense that a global element of the subobject classifier is false if and only if it is not true. However, it is not two-valued in the (classically equivalent) sense that every global element of the subobject classifier is either true or false.
          %h3#in_a_pretopos_or_coherent_category In a pretopos or coherent category
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is only a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+generator"} extremal generator
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:A\to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to B
            factors through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            is an isomorphism. In a category with a subobject classifier (such as a topos), any generator is a extremal generator.
          %p
            This strengthening is important in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative mathematics
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} category of sheaves
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %h3#in_a_lextensive_category In a lextensive category
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is only a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lextensive+category"} lextensive category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
            without
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+sets"} quotient sets
            (as commonly found in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntactic+category"} syntactic category
            of an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is well-pointed if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is only a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} noninitial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indecomposable+object"} indecomposable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+generator"} extremal generator
          %h2#as_an_axiom_schema_of_separation As an axiom schema of separation
          %p
            Well-pointedness in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+category"} Boolean category
            (if using
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
            (if using
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            being a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+generator"} strong generator
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+schema+of+bounded+separation"} axiom schema of bounded separation
          %p Let us define the following
          %ul
            %li
              A
              = succeed "-variable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
              variable.
            %li
              A
              = succeed "-context" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
              = succeed "-variables" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
            %li
              An
              = succeed "-atomic" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
            %li
              A
              = succeed "-quantifier" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
              = succeed "-variable." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
            %li
              A formula whose only atomic subformulas are
              = succeed "-atomic" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
              = succeed "-quantifiers" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
              = succeed "-formula." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+category"} Boolean category
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is well-pointed if
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in \mathrm{Ob}(\mathcal{E})
                is a strong generator: given objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathrm{Ob}(\mathcal{E})
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in \mathrm{Ob}(\mathcal{E})
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:A \hookrightarrow B
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:1 \to B
                there exists a global element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:1 \to A
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi y
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \circ y = x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+schemata+of+bounded+separation"} axiom schemata of bounded separation
                holds for
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+elements"} global elements
                = succeed "-formula" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x)
                with global element free variable
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:1 \to B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathrm{Ob}(\mathcal{E})
                and a monomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:A \hookrightarrow B
                such that for any global element
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:1 \to B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x)
                holds if and only if there exists a global element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:1 \to A
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi y
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \circ y = x
          %p
            In fact, given that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
            %strong well-pointed Boolean category
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %strong well-pointed Heyting category
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Improper subsets: given a subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq B
                with chosen
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:A \hookrightarrow B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in B
                there exists an element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in A
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(y) = x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/improper+subset"} improper subset
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            %li
              %p
                Bounded separation: for any
                = succeed "-formula" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x)
                with free variable
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in B
